3. User Personas

The digital insurance experience mainly supports the following user personas:

3.1 Guest User

A new/unregistered user entering the digital experience.

Typical activities:

- Obtain a quote
- Bind a policy
- Retrieve a quote
- Save and return later
- Create an online account
- Eventually sign in and continue the process

3.2 Signed-In User

An existing customer/user who already has an online account.

Typical activities:

- Access existing policies
- Manage policies
- Perform self-service activities
- Add additional products/add-ons
- Continue an existing quote or transaction

Persona Summary

Persona| Description
Guest User| New user entering the digital experience
Signed-In User| Existing customer with an online account
Existing Customer| Customer who can manage existing insurance policies

---

4. Insurance Portal – Main Capabilities

The insurance portal provides self-service functionality.

Quote & Bind

- Customer can obtain an insurance quote.
- Customer can proceed with binding the policy.

Manage Your Policy

For existing customers:

- View/manage existing policies
- Perform policy-related self-service activities

Add-Ons

- Add additional products/coverages to an existing or new policy, depending on eligibility.

---

5. Digital Insurance Flow

The high-level process captured during KT is:

Quote → Bind → Retrieve → Save & Return → Online Account Creation → Sign In

Detailed Flow

1. Quote
   
   - Customer starts the insurance quoting process.

2. Bind
   
   - Customer proceeds with binding the selected insurance product.

3. Retrieve
   
   - Customer can retrieve an existing quote/transaction.

4. Save & Return
   
   - Customer can save the current progress and return later.

5. Online Account Creation
   
   - A guest user can create an online account.

6. Sign In
   
   - Once the account is created, the user can sign in and continue using the digital services.

